PrismCheck - a report about PrismRTG on your Amiga
==================================================

If PrismRTG misbehaves on your machine, or you try it on hardware or an
emulator it has not been tested on, PrismCheck collects what is needed to
find out why - in one text file you can attach to a GitHub issue.

Use
  1. Install PrismRTG and reboot, so that PrismD is running.
  2. Double-click PrismCheck (or in a Shell: CD to this drawer, then
     Execute PrismCheck).
  3. It opens and closes a few test screens for 2 to 5 minutes, then asks
     whether to measure drawing speed too (another few minutes - say yes if
     you can).
  4. The report is RAM:PrismCheck-report.txt, and a copy is put in this
     drawer. Attach it to an issue at
         https://github.com/lainejones/PrismRTG/issues
     and say in a few words what you saw on the screen.

What it does
  Reads: the OS and library versions, CPU, memory, expansion boards,
  PrismRTG's version and settings, the monitor files, whether Picasso96 is
  installed too, the front screen and pointer.
  Tests: PrismRTG's drawing tests at 8, 16, 24 and 32 bits (each line should
  end in "0 wrong"), the Picasso96 API test, and a video-memory test
  (vramcheck - should say "0 of 40 copies wrong").
  Changes nothing: it writes only the report, in RAM: and in this drawer.

If something goes wrong half way (the Amiga hangs), RAM:PrismCheck-report.txt
is lost with the reset - in that case, say which step was on the screen.

Tools/ holds the test programs; each can also be run on its own.

